export anchor ArchiveVaultStyle:
    number: 410
    screen: DatabaseConsole
    name: Archive vault
    idea: The console is a dark reading room, where tables are labelled cabinet drawers, the open drawer shows its columns as index cards, the query is a typed request slip, results are ledger entries and history is a row of stamped call slips.
    base: dark
    palette:
        vault: #14100c, the page
        wood: #2a1e15, the cabinet, the nameplate and the style sheet
        drawer: #35281d, drawer fronts and swatch cells
        drawerEdge: #4a3829, drawer and cabinet edges
        card: #2b2720, index cards, the request slip and call slips
        ledger: #1b201a, the ledger page, with rules in #3b4636
        brass: #dbb86c, label holders, pulls, the title, keywords, Submit and focus
        onBrass: #2a1c06, text on brass
        cream: #f1e6cc, text
        muted: #c4b593, labels, column types and meta
        margin: #e8917f, the ledger margin rule
        ok: #a9d68f, the FILED stamp
        bad: #f19a88, the REJECTED stamp and its reason
    type:
        Old style serif for prose, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
        Palatino, Georgia, at 16px and 1.5. Typewriter for slips and cards,
        American Typewriter, Courier Prime, Courier New. The nameplate title
        is 26px small caps in brass, card titles 22px italic, section labels
        13px caps at 0.18em, ledger counts 18px typewriter.
    layout:
        A brass framed nameplate with a double inner rule shows Brightwork
        Data in small caps and Reading room for production-replica. Three
        pieces of furniture follow. On the left a 290px wooden card cabinet
        holds five drawers, each with a brass bordered label holder and a
        round pull. The tasks drawer is pulled out with a ledge below, its
        holder filled with brass, and six tabbed index cards inside, one per
        column with its type. In the middle the request slip, numbered
        0941, has the italic title Overdue tasks by project, a one line
        plain description, the SQL typed on ruled lines, and Submit request
        and Keep on file buttons. On the right a ledger page with a red
        margin line titled Entries returned, Entered in 38 ms, ruled rows
        with tally marks and counts, and a double ruled total of 3 rows
        entered. Below, a call slip log of three cards, each with time and
        name, two stamped FILED with a tick and the duration, the last
        stamped REJECTED in a tilted double box with the reason. A ruled
        brass plaque ends the screen with the three status facts. Below
        1100px the ledger moves under the slip, and on phones everything
        stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px gutters between furniture, 10px between drawers, 4px between cards.
    density: Medium. Three pieces of furniture, then the slip log.
    corners: Nearly square, 2 to 6px. Round drawer pulls and tabbed cards.
    borders: 2px brass label holders, double rules on the slip edge and the ledger total, one red margin line.
    shadows: Deep soft black shadows under the cabinet, slip and ledger, and a hard ledge under the open drawer.
    icons:
        Objects instead of icons. Drawer pulls, card tabs, tally marks and
        ink stamps with a tick for FILED or a cross for REJECTED.
    focus: A 3px double brass outline offset 3px.
    tone: Archivist wording, such as Request slip, Submit request, Entries returned and FILED.
